      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Two checks keep a van fleet legal. The driver's daily walkaround. The mechanic's planned maintenance. Miss one and DVSA can mark you down.</p><p>This is a plain <strong>fleet vehicle inspection checklist UK</strong> assessors can use today. It <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">works in any country</a> WhatsApp does.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>The daily walkaround is the driver's legal job, not the mechanic's.</li><li>This checklist covers what DVSA expects a driver to check.</li><li>Planned maintenance is the mechanic's job. Often every 6 weeks or 10,000 miles.</li><li>Write defects down. Do not keep them in your head.</li><li>A digital record with a time and a name beats paper in a visit.</li><li>Keep both records. Be able to show them.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The distinction",
      "heading": "Walkaround or planned maintenance?",
      "html": "<p>People mix these up. That leaves gaps.</p><p>The <strong>walkaround</strong> is the driver's check before the van moves. Tyres, lights, mirrors, fluids, glass, bodywork and load. No tools. Three to five minutes.</p><p>The <strong>planned maintenance</strong> is the mechanic's job at set times. Often every 6 weeks or 10,000 miles for busy vans. Brakes, suspension and steering.</p><p>A driver cannot see brake pads from the wheel arch. A mechanic cannot see if the load was tied down at 6am. Neither replaces the other.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The walkaround",
      "heading": "What the driver checks",
      "html": "<p>Do this before each journey. Photograph any defect. Report it before the van moves.</p><p><strong>Tyres:</strong> tread at least 1.6mm across the middle three-quarters. Many firms act at 3mm. Pressure as on the label, checked cold. No cuts or bulges. All wheel nuts there.</p><p><strong>Lights:</strong> dipped and main beam, side lights, brake lights, indicators, hazards, reversing light, number plate light. All clean and working.</p><p><strong>Fluids, by eye:</strong> oil, coolant and brake fluid between the marks. Washer bottle full. AdBlue not low.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The walkaround",
      "heading": "Body, load and cab",
      "html": "<p><strong>Body and glass:</strong> no chip in the driver's line of sight. Mirrors whole and set. Photograph new damage. Doors close and latch.</p><p><strong>Load:</strong> tools and materials cannot move. Racking firm. Not overloaded.</p><p><strong>Cab:</strong> no warning lights after start. Horn, wipers, handbrake and seatbelt work.</p><p><strong>Record it:</strong> date, driver name, registration and what you found. A check with no record is not evidence.</p>"
    },
    {
