      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is the difference between a walkaround and planned maintenance?</h3><p>The walkaround is the driver's check before each journey. Lights, tyres, fluids, body and load. Planned maintenance is the mechanic's job at set times. It covers what the driver cannot see.</p><h3>Who does the daily walkaround?</h3><p>The driver. The operator must give them a way to report defects, and act on them.</p><h3>What is the legal tyre tread minimum for vans?</h3><p>1.6mm across the middle three-quarters of the tread, all the way round. Many fleets act at 3mm.</p><h3>Must the checklist be signed?</h3><p>No signature is required by law. DVSA expects the record to show who did the check, and when. See the <a href=\"/pages/van-check-app-uk.html\">van check app for UK fleets</a> and the <a href=\"/pages/dvsa-walkaround-check-free-template-uk.html\">DVSA walkaround check free template</a>.</p>"
